# Secrets template. Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) and fill in:
#
#     cp .env.example .env.local
#
# The orchestrator and `cargo run` load it with `source .env.local`;
# the LIVE run sources `.env` instead (same keys). API keys come from
# the environment only, never from tamako.toml (specs.md Section 13).

# OpenRouter API key (https://openrouter.ai) — tamako.toml's global
# llm_base_url targets OpenRouter, so digest/embedding/caption ride
# this key. (An Opencode-family key here 401s those purposes silently
# into the retry path; the live launch line is the authoritative value
# source when the two diverge.)
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Only needed if you also use an anthropic-compatible endpoint
# (e.g. MiniMax/Qwen models on Opencode Go, or Anthropic first-party).
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Only needed for --live mode against real Telegram.
# TELOXIDE_TOKEN=

# Live-mode operator overrides (the container env file of
# migration-runbook.md Section 6 is hand-merged from `.env` plus these;
# they fail SILENT when absent — unset or empty-after-trim both
# count as unset, so this template is the checked-in source of truth
# for the required key set). Trailing annotations live on their own
# comment lines: the real env file is strict NAME=value only (podman
# keeps inline comments literal):
# TAMAKO_GATE_LLM_API_KEY=
# TAMAKO_REPLY_LLM_API_KEY=
# TAMAKO_SUMMARY_MODEL=
# diverges from the compiled minimax-m3 default:
# TAMAKO_CAPTION_MODEL=
# decision 84's prompt-cache affinity prefix:
# TAMAKO_LLM_SESSION_ID=
